     "\r\n<a style=\"font-weight:bold\" href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/secr/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/secr/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486261030000&amp;usg=AOvVaw20QnIc4G_CpkhCady7Lv0k\">secr</a>\r\n5.2.0 fixes minor bugs in derived(), sim.capthist()  and\r\naddCovariates(), and a more significant bug in region.N() (R.N ignored\r\nmodel for density). secr.fit() now allows (relative) density to be\r\nmodelled when maximising the conditional likelihood (CL = TRUE) - see the section on relative density in <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-densitysurfaces.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-densitysurfaces.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486261030000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3NmvJgA9dZH_J8QjsdTIzN\">secr-densitysurfaces.pdf</a>.\r\nAll changes are listed <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/secr%205.2.0%20NEWS.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/secr%25205.2.0%2520NEWS.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792486261030000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0WbMA0PNuHEMeCkPHzD8Fq\">here</a>.\r\n\r\n"
